  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1056 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will persist over the Southeast to begin the \nlong term period; however, synoptic guidance suggests that the upper \ntrough over the eastern seaboard will amplify by late week and \nattempt to push westward into the South. Although, uncertainty \nremains if this feature will push far enough west to have much of an \neffect on the local area. This is due to the stout ridge over the \ncentral CONUS that looks to be pushed eastward over our region Friday\ninto Saturday by a progressive trough over the western CONUS. \nMeanwhile, surface high pressure looks to largely maintain its hold \nover much of the eastern CONUS through the first part of next \nweekend. Overall, with continued subsidence from surface high \npressure and proximity of upper ridging, the current forecast remains\ndevoid of rain chances through at least early next weekend. In \naddition, the Fall-like weather continues with forecast highs in the \nmid to upper 70s and lows mainly in the mid to upper 40s.",
